  "type": "dragdrop",
  "correctLetters": [],
  "en": {
   "stem": "You are designing two Microsoft Copilot Studio agents named Agent1 and Agent2. Each agent must meet\nthe following requirements:\nEach agent must use a standard model.\nEach agent must NOT use generative orchestration.\nAgent1 must support simple and short phrases for a given topic.\nAgent2 must integrate with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Contact Center voice channel.\n\nYou need to recommend language models for the agents.\nWhat should you recommend for each agent? To answer, drag the appropriate language models to the\ncorrect agents. Each language model may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to\ndrag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.",
   "options": {},
   "scenario": "",
   "explanation": "Explanation:\nBox 1: Natural Language Understanding (NLU) \nAgent1 must support simple and short phrases for a given topic.\nFor a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that must not use generative orchestration and requires support for\nsimple, short trigger phrases, the best choice is the Classic NLU (Natural Language Understanding)\nmodel. \nWhen you disable generative orchestration (also known as \"Generative mode\" or \"Generative AI\"\norchestration), the agent reverts to Classic orchestration. In this mode, the agent relies on predefined\ntrigger phrases to map user input directly to specific topics.\nBox 2: Natural Language Understanding +  (NLU +)\nAgent2 must integrate with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Contact Center voice channel.\nFor a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent using classic orchestration (no generative orchestration) and\nintegrating with the Dynamics 365 Contact Center voice channel, the best language model is NLU+. \nWhy NLU+ is the Best Choice\nWhile standard agents offer three \"classic\" Natural Language Understanding (NLU) options, NLU+ is\nspecifically designed for high-performance, enterprise-grade scenarios like voice channels.\nNote:\nComparison of Classic Models \n\nReference:"
  },
  "zh": {
   "stem": "您正在设计两个名为Agent1和Agent2的Microsoft Copilot Studio代理。每个代理必须满足\n以下要求：\n每个代理必须使用标准模型。\n每个代理不得使用生成性编排。\n代理1必须支持给定主题的简单和简短短语。\n代理2必须与Microsoft Dynamics 365联系中心语音通道集成。\n您需要为代理推荐语言模型。\n您应该为每个代理推荐什么？要回答此问题，请将适当的语言模型拖动到正确的代理上。每个语言模型\n可以使用一次、使用多次或根本不使用。您可能需要\\拖动窗格之间的分隔条或滚动以查看内容。",
   "options": {},
   "scenario": "",
   "explanation": "解释：\n框1：自然语言理解（NLU）\n代理1必须支持给定主题的简单和简短短语。\n对于一个不得使用生成性编排且需要支持简单、短触发短语的Microsoft Copilot Studio代理，最佳选择\n是经典自然语言理解（NLU）模型。\n当您禁用生成性编排（也称为“生成模式”或“生成AI”编排）时，代理将恢复为经典编排。在\n此模式下，代理依赖于预定义的触发短语将用户输入直接映射到特定主题。\n框2：自然语言理解+（NLU +）\n代理2必须与Microsoft Dynamics 365联系中心语音通道集成。\n对于使用经典编排（不使用生成编排）并与 Dynamics 365 联系中心语音通道集成的 Microsoft Co\npilot Studio 代理，最佳语言模型是 NLU+。\n为什么 NLU+ 是最佳选择\n虽然标准代理提供三种“经典”自然语言理解（NLU）选项，但 NLU+ 专门为高性能、企业级场景（\n如语音通道）而设计。\n注意：\n经典模型比较\n参考："
  },
