  "en": {
   "stem": "A company has a Microsoft Power Platform environment.\nYou need to build two agents named Agent1 and Agent2. The solution must meet the following\nrequirements:\nAgent1 must be extendable by using the Semantic Kernel and must connect to multiple business apps\nand APIs.\nAgent2 must connect directly to data stored in Microsoft Dataverse and must be embeddable in a\nMicrosoft Power Apps canvas app.\n[Not D]\n\nWhat should you use to build each agent? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.",
   "options": {},
   "scenario": "",
   "explanation": "Explanation:\nBox 1: Microsoft Copilot Studio\nAgent1 must be extendable by using the Semantic Kernel and must connect to multiple business apps and\nAPIs.\nTo build a Microsoft AI agent that integrates Semantic Kernel and connects to various business systems\nwithin the Power Platform, you will use Microsoft Copilot Studio as your primary orchestration hub.\nBy combining these technologies, you bridge the gap between \"low-code\" conversational interfaces and\n\"pro-code\" LLM orchestration.\nAPI。\n\nThe Architecture\nTo reach your goal, you will follow a multi-tier integration strategy:\nMicrosoft Copilot Studio: Acts as the \"Frontend\" and dialog manager.\nSemantic Kernel (SDK): Acts as the \"Brain\" hosted in an Azure function or web app.\nPower Platform Connectors: Act as the \"Hands\" to talk to 1,200+ apps.\nCustom APIs: Connected via Semantic Kernel \"Plugins\" or Copilot Studio \"Actions.\"\nBox 2: Microsoft Copilot Studio\nAgent2 must connect directly to data stored in Microsoft Dataverse and must be embeddable in a\nMicrosoft Power Apps canvas app.\nTo build a Microsoft AI agent that connects to Dataverse and is embedded in a Power Apps canvas app,\nyou need to use Microsoft Copilot Studio as the primary development platform. \nTechnical Requirements\nTo get started, ensure your environment meets these core prerequisites:\nCopilot Studio Solution: Your environment must have version 2.0.0.649.1 or higher.\nDataverse Database: The environment must contain a provisioned Microsoft Dataverse database.\nAdmin Settings: A tenant administrator must enable \"Publish Copilots with AI features\" in the Power\nPlatform admin center.\nUnmanaged Customizations: Ensure that the \"block unmanaged customizations\" setting is disabled in your\nenvironment.\nIncorrect:\n* Azure Logic Apps\nWhile Logic Apps can connect to Dataverse, they are a workflow orchestration tool (similar to Power\nAutomate) and do not provide the conversational AI interface or the embedding capabilities required for an\n\"agent.\"\n* Microsoft Foundry\nThis is not a standard component of the Power Platform for building AI agents; it usually refers to internal\nMicrosoft data management tools or unrelated external products.\n* Copilot in Power Apps\n This refers to the AI assistant that helps makers build apps or helps users query data through a\npredefined side pane, but it is not the tool used to build a standalone, customizable agent that you embed\nyourself.\nCopilot in Power Apps is an AI-powered assistant, driven by Azure OpenAI Service, that enables users to\ncreate, modify, and manage business applications using natural language instead of code. It allows\ndevelopers of all skill levels to instantly build apps, design data models, and generate complex formulas by\nsimply describing their needs in everyday language.\nReference:"
  },
  "zh": {
   "stem": "一家公司拥有一个 Microsoft Power Platform 环境。\n您需要构建两个代理，分别命名为 Agent1 和 Agent2。解决方案必须满足以下\n要求：\nAgent1 必须可以通过使用语义内核进行扩展，并且必须连接到多个业务应用程序\n和 API。\nAgent2 必须直接连接到存储在 Microsoft Dataverse 中的数据，并且必须可以嵌入到\nMicrosoft Power Apps 画布应用中。\n您应该使用什么来构建每个代理？要回答，请在答案区域选择适当的选项。",
   "options": {},
   "scenario": "",
   "explanation": "解释：\n框 1：Microsoft Copilot Studio\nAgent1 必须可以通过使用语义内核进行扩展，并且必须连接到多个业务应用程序和\n要构建一个集成语义内核并连接到 Power Platform 中各种业务系统的 Microsoft AI 代理，您将使用 Micr\nosoft Copilot Studio 作为您的主要编排中心。\n通过结合这些技术，您可以弥合“低代码”对话界面与“专业代码”大型语言模型编排之间的差距。\n架构\n为了实现您的目标，您将遵循多层集成策略：\nMicrosoft Copilot Studio：充当“前端”和对话管理器。\n语义内核（SDK）：充当“大脑”，托管在 Azure 函数或 Web 应用中。\nPower Platform 连接器：充当与 1,200 多个应用程序对话的“手”。\n自定义 API：通过语义内核“插件”或 Copilot Studio“操作”连接。\n框 2：Microsoft Copilot Studio\nAgent2 必须直接连接到存储在 Microsoft Dataverse 中的数据，并且必须可以嵌入到\nMicrosoft Power Apps 画布应用中。\n要构建一个连接到 Dataverse 并嵌入在 Power Apps 画布应用中的 Microsoft AI 代理，\n您需要使用 Microsoft Copilot Studio 作为主要开发平台。\n技术要求\n要开始，请确保您的环境满足以下核心前提条件：\nCopilot Studio 解决方案：您的环境必须具有版本 2.0.0.649.1 或更高版本。\nDataverse 数据库：环境中必须包含一个已配置的 Microsoft Dataverse 数据库。\n管理员设置：租户管理员必须在 Power\nPlatform 管理中心启用“发布具有 AI 功能的 Copilot”。\n未管理的自定义：确保在您的环境中禁用“阻止未管理的自定义”设置。\n不正确：\n* Azure 逻辑应用\n虽然逻辑应用可以连接到数据平台，但它们是一个工作流编排工具（类似于 PowerAutomate），并\n不提供所需的对话式 AI 接口或嵌入能力来支持“代理”。\n* 微软创意工坊\n这不是构建 AI 代理的 Power Platform 的标准组件；它通常指的是内部的微软数据管理工具或无关的外部\n产品。\n* Power Apps中的Copilot\n这指的是帮助制造者构建应用程序的人工智能助手，或者帮助用户通过预定义的侧边栏查询数据\n，但它不是用于构建一个独立的、可定制的代理工具，您需要自己嵌入。\nPower Apps中的Copilot是一个由Azure OpenAI服务驱动的人工智能助手，使用户能够使用自然语言而非\n代码来创建、修改和管理业务应用程序。它允许所有技能水平的开发人员通过简单描述他们的需求\n，以日常语言即时构建应用程序、设计数据模型和生成复杂公式。\n参考："
  },
