  "en": {
   "stem": "A company deploys a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent that integrates with a Microsoft Power Automate\ndesktop flow.\nYou need to recommend a testing solution that meets the following requirements:\nTest cases must validate the most recent changes to the agent before the agent is released.\nThe flow must be validated as part of the agent's orchestration.\nWhat should you recommend for each requirement? To answer, select the appropriate options in the\nanswer area.",
   "options": {},
   "scenario": "",
   "explanation": "Explanation:\nBox 1: Run test against the latest unpublished version of the agent\nTest cases must validate the most recent changes to the agent before the agent is released.\nTo validate the most recent changes to a Microsoft Copilot Studio agent integrated with a Power Automate\ndesktop flow before release, use the Copilot Studio Kit. \n \nThis specialized toolkit allows you to create and automate test cases that run against the test version of\nyour agent rather than the published one.\nKey Components for Validation\nCopilot Studio Kit: Use this to build test sets (sets of questions and expected answers) and run them\nthrough a graphical interface.\nPower Platform Pipelines: Integrate your tests into a deployment pipeline. The pipeline can be configured\nto automatically trigger these test runs whenever a deployment request is made, acting as a quality gate\nthat pauses the release if tests fail.\n\n*-> Agent Configuration: In the kit, specify the development environment as the source so that the tests\ninteract with your latest unpublished changes.\nDesktop Flow Verification: Since your agent uses desktop flows, use the Response match and Plan\nvalidation test types within the kit to ensure the agent correctly triggers the integrated flow tools as part of\nits execution plan.\nBox 2: Use the Power Automate for desktop console\nThe flow must be validated as part of the agent's orchestration.\nTo ensure your Microsoft Power Automate desktop flow is correctly validated for orchestration within a\nMicrosoft Copilot Studio agent, follow these steps using the Power Automate for desktop console and the\nCopilot Studio designer:\n1. Validate via Power Automate for Desktop Console \nRun a Local Test: Open the Power Automate for desktop console, select your flow, and click the Start\nbutton to run it as a \"local attended\" flow. This confirms that the logic and UI selectors work correctly in\nyour environment.\nCheck Variables: Ensure that any Input and Output variables are properly defined. These are critical for\npassing data between the cloud-based agent and the desktop machine.\nMonitor Connectivity: Use the Troubleshooter within the console (under Help > Troubleshooter) to\ndiagnose any connectivity issues with the cloud runtime, ensuring the agent can trigger the desktop flow. \n \n2. Validate the Integration in Copilot Studio\nReference:"
  },
  "zh": {
   "stem": "一家公司部署了一个与Microsoft Power Automate桌面流程集成的Microsoft Copilot Studio代理。\n您需要推荐一个满足以下要求的测试解决方案：\n测试用例必须在代理发布之前验证对代理的最新更改。\n该流程必须作为代理编排的一部分进行验证。\n您应该为每个要求推荐什么？要回答，请在答案区域选择适当的选项。",
   "options": {},
   "scenario": "",
   "explanation": "解释：\n框1：针对代理的最新未发布版本运行测试\n测试用例必须在代理发布之前验证对代理的最新更改。\n要在发布之前验证与Power Automate桌面流程集成的Microsoft Copilot Studio代理的最新更改，请使用C\nopilot Studio工具包。\n这个专业工具包允许您创建和自动化测试用例，这些用例针对的是代理的测试版本，而不是已发布的版\n本。\n验证的关键组件\nCopilot Studio工具包：使用此工具包构建测试集（问题和预期答案的集合），并通过图形界面运行\n它们。\nPower Platform管道：将您的测试集成到部署管道中。该管道可以配置为在每次发出部署请求时自动触发\n这些测试运行，充当质量门控，如果测试失败则暂停发布。\n*-> 代理配置：在工具包中，将开发环境指定为源，以便测试\n与您最新未发布的更改进行交互。\n桌面流程验证：由于您的代理使用桌面流程，请在工具包中使用响应匹配和计划验证测试类型，以\n确保代理在其执行计划中正确触发集成流程工具。\n框2：使用 Power Automate 桌面控制台\n该流程必须作为代理编排的一部分进行验证。\n为了确保您的 Microsoft Power Automate 桌面流程在 Microsoft Copilot Studio 代理中正确验证以进\n行编排，请按照以下步骤使用 Power Automate 桌面控制台和 Copilot Studio 设计器：\n1. 通过 Power Automate 桌面控制台进行验证运行本\n地测试：打开 Power Automate 桌面控制台，选择您的流程，然后单击开始按钮将其作为“本地参与\n”流程运行。这确认了逻辑和 UI 选择器在您的环境中正常工作。\n检查变量：确保任何输入和输出变量正确定义。这对于在云端代理和桌面计算机之间传递数据至关重要\n监控连接性：使用控制台中的故障排除工具（在帮助 > 故障排除下）诊断与云运行时的任何连接问\n题，确保代理可以触发桌面流程。\n2. 在 Copilot Studio 中验证集成\n参考："
  },
